elease: prepare 0.5.0 qualified EIDOS Agent compatibility preview","tree":{"sha":"69959b83b8fc36efce96085ac54b2a2f115a2fe5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Computational-social-science/Eidos/git/trees/69959b83b8fc36efce96085ac54b2a2f115a2fe5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Computational-social-science/Eidos/git/commits/21e26b784604616a96648a615f48aa2747f35e7f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/commit/21e26b784604616a96648a615f48aa2747f35e7f","node_id":"C_kwDOVR8FZ9oAKDIxZTI2Yjc4NDYwNDYxNmE5NjY0OGE2MTVmNDhhYTI3NDdmMzVlN2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/commit/6b7f588eadb18970fcb61db72773e9f8d57eac92","sha":"6b7f588eadb18970fcb61db72773e9f8d57eac92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Computational-social-science/Eidos/commits/6b7f588eadb18970fcb61db72773e9f8d57eac92"}],"sha":"21e26b784604616a96648a615f48aa2747f35e7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Computational-social-science/Eidos/commits/21e26b784604616a96648a615f48aa2747f35e7f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Computational-social-science/Eidos/commits/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-11-04T04:01:28Z","email":"research@limen.org","name":"LIMEN Research"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-11-04T04:01:28Z","email":"research@limen.org","name":"LIMEN Research"},"message":"test(monitor): preserve virtual-environment entry in enrollment assertions","tree":{"sha":"49be4637a37c0a2f23b0d4f5f86b076cb8305164","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Computational-social-science/Eidos/git/trees/49be4637a37c0a2f23b0d4f5f86b076cb8305164"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Computational-social-science/Eidos/git/commits/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/commit/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae","node_id":"C_kwDOVR8FZ9oAKDA0NWM5ZTA4YjFmMGFjZWZmMmU2M2EyM2FiNzdlMTIxYzE0MWM2YWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/commit/21e26b784604616a96648a615f48aa2747f35e7f","sha":"21e26b784604616a96648a615f48aa2747f35e7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Computational-social-science/Eidos/commits/21e26b784604616a96648a615f48aa2747f35e7f"}],"sha":"045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Computational-social-science/Eidos/commits/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae"}],"diff_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/compare/6b7f588...045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae.diff","files":[{"additions":10,"blob_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/blob/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/README.md","changes":19,"contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Computational-social-science/Eidos/contents/README.md?ref=045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae","deletions":9,"filename":"README.md","patch":"@@ -1,10 +1,11 @@\n # EIDOS Agent \u2014 reusable research execution and evidence\n \n-**Version 0.5.0** \u00b7 unreleased development candidate \u00b7 local-first \u00b7 MIT framework\n+**Version 0.5.0** \u00b7 compatibility preview \u00b7 local-first \u00b7 MIT framework\n \n-Latest published release: [0.4.12](https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/releases/tag/v0.4.12).\n-The version above identifies development source, not a published 0.5.0 product.\n-Release-integrity checking still blocks the source/history mismatch.\n+Publication state and exact assets: [0.5.0 release record](https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/releases/tag/v0.5.0).\n+The delivery record binds source, exact-head CI, tag and qualified wheel bytes;\n+preparation alone does not establish publication. The existing local resident\n+monitor has its separate 0.4.12 runtime and is not upgraded by installing a worker.\n [Main-branch CI](https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/actions/workflows/ci.yml)\n is separate from candidate acceptance.\n \n@@ -22,16 +23,16 @@ should require a pinned core package and small project-local configuration.\n \n | Entry point | Availability and boundary |\n |---|---|\n-| SDK / release wheel | Published 0.4.12; explicit project registration, execution, verification and delivery |\n-| Installed project CLI | Unreleased candidate: init/check/status/report/feedback with retained installed trials |\n+| SDK / release wheel | Qualified 0.5.0 compatibility artifact; verify the actual release record before installation |\n+| Installed project CLI | init/check/status/report/feedback with retained Windows/Linux installed trials |\n | Shared worker observation | Candidate protocol, bounded source collector and UI tested; existing 8765 process not migrated |\n | Thin project Agent skill | Instruction adapter and CLI tool smoke; live Agent reasoning needs separate acceptance |\n | Public PyPI / generic MCP | Not delivered; naming, compatibility and adapter qualification remain open |\n-| Complete feedback / scientific RSI | Not established; originating-project release replay and held-out improvement remain open |\n+| Software feedback / scientific RSI | Protected real-origin preparation is VALIDATED; publication/adoption/replay remain pending until actual receipts. Scientific RSI needs separate held-out acceptance |\n \n Start with [project integration](docs/PROJECT_INTEGRATION.md), the English\n-[installed-candidate quickstart](https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/blob/feature/shared-monitor/docs/DOWNSTREAM-QUICKSTART.md)\n-and [delivery plan](https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/blob/feature/shared-monitor/docs/REUSE-DELIVERY-PLAN.md).\n+[installed-worker quickstart](docs/DOWNSTREAM-QUICKSTART.md)\n+and [delivery plan](docs/REUSE-DELIVERY-PLAN.md).\n Do not run `pip install eidos` from PyPI for this framework: that name belongs to\n an unrelated astronomy package. Exact wheel/hash installation is a separate path.\n ","raw_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/raw/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/README.md","sha":"c9e449efcb8d0a261599c200553a3bbfbb098647","status":"modified"},{"additions":50,"blob_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/blob/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/docs%2FDOWNSTREAM-QUICKSTART.md","changes":50,"contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Computational-social-science/Eidos/contents/docs%2FDOWNSTREAM-QUICKSTART.md?ref=045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae","deletions":0,"filename":"docs/DOWNSTREAM-QUICKSTART.md","patch":"@@ -1,5 +1,55 @@\n # Reuse EIDOS in an independent research project\n \n+## Current compatibility delivery, 2026-11-04\n+\n+The current qualified worker is **EIDOS Agent 0.5.0**, distribution `eidos`,\n+import namespace `framework`, consoles `eidos-agent` and `eidos`. Check the\n+[actual public release](https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/releases/tag/v0.5.0)\n+before downloading: source preparation or a version record is not publication.\n+The exact 51-module wheel passes native Windows and same-host offline Linux\n+numerical, lifecycle and recovery-shell acceptance. This supersedes the older\n+candidate selection below. The existing resident monitor remains separately on\n+0.4.12; installing a worker does not start or migrate it.\n+\n+Ordinary projects need neither a source fork nor a full checkout at execution\n+time. Use Python 3.12 and uv in a new, dedicated runtime directory. Preserve an\n+existing study's CUDA/PyTorch environment. Download the published wheel and the\n+frozen core requirements from its immutable tag, and verify both hashes before\n+installation. PowerShell, substituting actual absolute paths:\n+\n+```powershell\n+$runtime = '<new dedicated runtime directory>'\n+$project = '<existing research project root>'\n+New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $runtime -ErrorAction Stop | Out-Null\n+$wheel = Join-Path $runtime 'eidos-0.5.0-py3-none-any.whl'\n+$requirements = Join-Path $runtime 'core-requirements.txt'\n+Invoke-WebRequest 'https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/releases/download/v0.5.0/eidos-0.5.0-py3-none-any.whl' -OutFile $wheel\n+Invoke-WebRequest 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/v0.5.0/reference/numerical_programs_acceptance/recorded_trials/v0.5.0/input-linux/core-requirements.txt' -OutFile $requirements\n+if ((Get-FileHash $wheel -Algorithm SHA256).Hash -ne '56d2fe35b1e5ab552fe001ae675e3af4f095e78522fa8fae682f5ea41cfa301c') { throw 'Wheel identity mismatch' }\n+if ((Get-FileHash $requirements -Algorithm SHA256).Hash -ne 'ca27b7da8739f5e3f1d14e54a6172b1bc9bb9da9e4344b1103d9216b2378e5de') { throw 'Dependency lock identity mismatch' }\n+uv venv --python 3.12 (Join-Path $runtime 'venv')\n+$workerPy = Join-Path $runtime 'venv/Scripts/python.exe'\n+uv pip install --link-mode copy --python $workerPy --require-hashes -r $requirements\n+uv pip install --link-mode copy --python $workerPy --no-deps $wheel\n+& $workerPy -I -m framework.cli --help\n+& $workerPy -I -m framework.cli init --project $project --json\n+```\n+\n+On Linux use `venv/bin/python`; retain that venv entry rather than resolving its\n+base-interpreter symlink. These downloads require public network access; runtime\n+qualification itself can be offline. No model service, paid API or credential is\n+required for the core path. Initial scientific acceptance is deliberately REFUSED;\n+configure the project's own validator and declared inputs before running `check`.\n+Use the selected interpreter for `check/status/report/feedback`, as shown below.\n+Scientific validators and Quarto/TeX/Poppler prerequisites remain project-owned.\n+\n+The software repair campaign is documented in [feedback lifecycle](FEEDBACK-LIFECYCLE.md).\n+Use actual journal receipts to distinguish VALIDATED, RELEASED, ADOPTED, REPLAYED\n+and CLOSED. An installed package or Agent adapter alone cannot close a defect or\n+qualify scientific RSI. Public PyPI `eidos` belongs to an unrelated project.\n+\n+## Historical development checkpoints\n+\n Status: 2026-11-03. Stable release: **0.4.12**. The installed project CLI and\n shared-worker protocol below are **unreleased 0.5.0 development**. Installing a\n worker wheel does not install or migrate the complete monitor service.","raw_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/raw/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/docs%2FDOWNSTREAM-QUICKSTART.md","sha":"5407e36256c2412c56e233ef8e95dd39ae08c441","status":"modified"},{"additions":11,"blob_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/blob/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/docs%2FEVOLUTION.json","changes":18,"contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Computational-social-science/Eidos/contents/docs%2FEVOLUTION.json?ref=045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae","deletions":7,"filename":"docs/EVOLUTION.json","patch":"@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@\n {\n-  \"asof\": \"2026-11-04T10:14:21+08:00\",\n+  \"asof\": \"2026-11-04T11:34:33+08:00\",\n   \"version\": \"0.5.0\",\n   \"state\": {\n     \"chains\": {\n@@ -51,16 +51,12 @@\n     \"open_defects\": 0\n   },\n   \"evolution\": {\n-    \"mutation_runs\": 2,\n+    \"mutation_runs\": 6,\n     \"runs_with_a_blind_spot\": 0,\n     \"blind_spots_found\": 0,\n     \"blind_spots_open\": 0,\n-    \"releases\": 22,\n+    \"releases\": 23,\n     \"tests_by_release\": [\n-      {\n-        \"version\": \"0.4.7\",\n-        \"tests\": 786\n-      },\n       {\n         \"version\": \"0.4.8\",\n         \"tests\": 876\n@@ -80,9 +76,17 @@\n       {\n         \"version\": \"0.4.12\",\n         \"tests\": 1208\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \"version\": \"0.5.0\",\n+        \"tests\": 1365\n       }\n     ],\n     \"blind_spots_by_run\": [\n+      0,\n+      0,\n+      0,\n+      0,\n       0,\n       0\n     ]","raw_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/raw/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/docs%2FEVOLUTION.json","sha":"8f8e837d3cc0f38cfe1ac9016aea161b489f3725","status":"modified"},{"additions":15,"blob_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/blob/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/docs%2FFEEDBACK-LIFECYCLE.md","changes":15,"contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Computational-social-science/Eidos/contents/docs%2FFEEDBACK-LIFECYCLE.md?ref=045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae","deletions":0,"filename":"docs/FEEDBACK-LIFECYCLE.md","patch":"@@ -147,3 +147,18 @@ The same 51-module wheel also passes the current native Windows and isolated\n Linux numerical/lifecycle/recovery-shell acceptance. Linux additionally checks\n both console aliases and the old/repaired private probe. The current artifact's\n Linux evidence is now independent of the earlier wheel's historical profile.\n+\n+### First exact-head CI refusal and test-contract correction\n+\n+The first delivery head `21e26b784604616a96648a615f48aa2747f35e7f` passed the\n+Windows/Linux installed-SDK workflow but failed both Linux source suites. The\n+registration test incorrectly resolved the venv launch entry to the base Python,\n+contrary to the existing SDK and deployment contract. Publication stopped before\n+tagging. An independent normal-installed, network-disabled Linux replay retained\n+the original one-failure/four-pass result. Correcting the expected launch entry\n+and independently asserting the actual worker prefix yields five passes on\n+Linux and five on Windows. Both focused independent reviews approve the change.\n+The wheel, SDK and sealed campaign producer/policy are unchanged. Frozen raw CI\n+annotations, old/new test inputs and actual execution evidence are retained in\n+`reference/shared_monitor_acceptance/recorded_trials/venv-entry-ci-v1`.\n+Remote CI must pass the new exact delivery head before publication can proceed.","raw_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/raw/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/docs%2FFEEDBACK-LIFECYCLE.md","sha":"8d18aac80303cf27796b2482331103fc83ded402","status":"modified"},{"additions":14,"blob_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/blob/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/docs%2FSCREENS.json","changes":28,"contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Computational-social-science/Eidos/contents/docs%2FSCREENS.json?ref=045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae","deletions":14,"filename":"docs/SCREENS.json","patch":"@@ -5,13 +5,13 @@\n   },\n   \"scale\": 2,\n   \"sources\": {\n-    \"dashboard.html\": \"56742f5f0672fa7567926a3d24ced035215410b5a4d5918ddb252067f78d22fd\",\n-    \"index.html\": \"beb6ae099403c38b78dac6d8bb046f9c2d1a3fdf3ce90ff3bd8faad01beaede9\"\n+    \"dashboard.html\": \"ce70579913ab434fde39305732c927e3b4176a482b5dee992ea3c74d993ab916\",\n+    \"index.html\": \"6f6c622e6079d793393dc5eac2c51fd3eb6b4f52c63397dbaf0182bbaf1d116f\"\n   },\n   \"images\": {\n     \"dashboard-top\": {\n-      \"sha256\": \"d35ea4272a661ec1bfdd16a0042d642dfff7abb0610bf27ccd00fc2b0a455d1b\",\n-      \"bytes\": 264720\n+      \"sha256\": \"7c87577d4d750b802b0867208af4cf9e7b41a39637715b1a25899aa24da710b6\",\n+      \"bytes\": 263558\n     },\n     \"dashboard-operator\": {\n       \"sha256\": \"b106c695a7ea8f45e4ff4f622fe261ee9fa5713334f40ea97eb3a9987743b36d\",\n@@ -22,12 +22,12 @@\n       \"bytes\": 132610\n     },\n     \"dashboard-history\": {\n-      \"sha256\": \"a8dbea5409a2e75d40d1b8b1f01f78c310a3cbba55055154ee501d3bea0a1441\",\n-      \"bytes\": 76743\n+      \"sha256\": \"050f79293fa530af5539ca008e9fb27e19365d40b3866634b95aec64eed45e7b\",\n+      \"bytes\": 76645\n     },\n     \"index-top\": {\n-      \"sha256\": \"dddc6f9da60f16ca1cf264145a0313ec8706c8de488067987dfc7662651ba333\",\n-      \"bytes\": 419447\n+      \