e progress indicator</h3>\r\n@@ -190,16 +190,16 @@ <h2>Framework self-audit \u2014 chains \u00d7 modules \u00d7 service boundaries</h2>\n       With no active fault, repair stages are SKIP.</p>\r\n       <div class=\"matrix-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Recovery snapshot\"><svg class='operator-matrix' viewBox='0 0 1146 76' width='100%' role='img' aria-label='self-check and self-heal loop'><g class='node operator' data-operator='self-check \u00b7 sample' tabindex='0' role='button'><title>self-check \u00b7 sample \u00b7 IDLE \u00b7 15 s</title><rect x='4' y='6' width='168' height='50' rx='4' fill='#2a2f36' stroke='#0a0c0f'/><text x='13' y='25' font-size='11' fill='#e6e8eb'>self-check \u00b7 sample</text><text x='13' y='44' font-size='10' fill='#e6e8eb'>15 s</text></g><path d='M175 31 L195 31' stroke='#96a3b5' stroke-width='1.1' marker-end='url(#ah2)'/><g class='node operator' data-operator='derive verdict' tabindex='0' role='button'><title>derive verdict \u00b7 FAIL \u00b7 overall None contradicts 5 fault(s)</title><rect x='198' y='6' width='168' height='50' rx='4' fill='#e5534b' stroke='#0a0c0f'/><text x='207' y='25' font-size='11' fill='#ffffff'>derive verdict</text><text x='207' y='44' font-size='10' fill='#ffffff'>overall None contradicts</text></g><path d='M369 31 L389 31' stroke='#96a3b5' stroke-width='1.1' marker-end='url(#ah2)'/><g class='node operator' data-operator='plan repair' tabindex='0' role='button'><title>plan repair \u00b7 IDLE \u00b7 recovery.plan</title><rect x='392' y='6' width='168' height='50' rx='4' fill='#2a2f36' stroke='#0a0c0f'/><text x='401' y='25' font-size='11' fill='#e6e8eb'>plan repair</text><text x='401' y='44' font-size='10' fill='#e6e8eb'>recovery.plan</text></g><path d='M563 31 L583 31' stroke='#96a3b5' stroke-width='1.1' marker-end='url(#ah2)'/><g class='node operator' data-operator='execute' tabindex='0' role='button'><title>execute \u00b7 IDLE \u00b7 recovery.execute</title><rect x='586' y='6' width='168' height='50' rx='4' fill='#2a2f36' stroke='#0a0c0f'/><text x='595' y='25' font-size='11' fill='#e6e8eb'>execute</text><text x='595' y='44' font-size='10' fill='#e6e8eb'>recovery.execute</text></g><path d='M757 31 L777 31' stroke='#96a3b5' stroke-width='1.1' marker-end='url(#ah2)'/><g class='node operator' data-operator='verify' tabindex='0' role='button'><title>verify \u00b7 IDLE \u00b7 recovery.verify</title><rect x='780' y='6' width='168' height='50' rx='4' fill='#2a2f36' stroke='#0a0c0f'/><text x='789' y='25' font-size='11' fill='#e6e8eb'>verify</text><text x='789' y='44' font-size='10' fill='#e6e8eb'>recovery.verify</text></g><path d='M951 31 L971 31' stroke='#96a3b5' stroke-width='1.1' marker-end='url(#ah2)'/><g class='node operator' data-operator='record' tabindex='0' role='button'><title>record \u00b7 IDLE \u00b7 0 healed \u00b7 24 h</title><rect x='974' y='6' width='168' height='50' rx='4' fill='#2a2f36' stroke='#0a0c0f'/><text x='983' y='25' font-size='11' fill='#e6e8eb'>record</text><text x='983' y='44' font-size='10' fill='#e6e8eb'>0 healed \u00b7 24 h</text></g><path d='M1058.0 56 C1106 72, 40 72, 88.0 56' fill='none' stroke='#a9b6c8' stroke-width='1.2' opacity='0.85' stroke-dasharray='4 3' marker-end='url(#ah2)'/><defs><marker id='ah2' viewBox='0 0 10 10' refX='8.5' refY='5' markerWidth='4' markerHeight='4' orient='auto'><path d='M0 1 L9 5 L0 9 z' fill='context-stroke'/></marker></defs></svg></div></div>\r\n     <div class=\"opwrap\" id=\"evolution-snapshot\"><h3>Feedback \u2192 evolution \u2014 how a defect becomes a guard</h3>\r\n-      <p class=\"figure-note\">Historical ledger \u00b7 2026-11-04T10:14:21+08:00 \u00b7 workflow stages carry no live PASS verdict.</p>\r\n+      <p class=\"figure-note\">Historical ledger \u00b7 2026-11-04T11:34:33+08:00 \u00b7 workflow stages carry no live PASS verdict.</p>\r\n       <div class=\"matrix-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Evolution workflow\"><svg class='evolution-matrix' viewBox='0 0 1198 66' width='100%' role='img' aria-label='feedback to evolution cycle'><g class='stage' data-stage='1 FIND'><title>1 FIND \u00b7 6 instruments \u00b7 a mutation, a render, a dead endpoint</title><rect x='4' y='4' width='214' height='44' rx='4' fill='#1b2027' stroke='#2a3038'/><rect x='4' y='4' width='3' height='44' fill='#5b8def'/><text x='15' y='17' font-size='10' letter-spacing='0.08em' fill='#98a2b3'>1 FIND</text><text x='15' y='35' font-size='11' fill='#e6e8eb'>6 instruments</text></g><path d='M222 26 L244 26' stroke='#96a3b5' stroke-width='1.1' marker-end='url(#ah3)'/><g class='stage' data-stage='2 ENCODE'><title>2 ENCODE \u00b7 13 fixtures \u00b7 65 cases \u00b7 fixture \u00b7 mutation \u00b7 transition rule</title><rect x='248' y='4' width='214' height='44' rx='4' fill='#1b2027' stroke='#2a3038'/><rect x='248' y='4' width='3' height='44' fill='#5b8def'/><text x='259' y='17' font-size='10' letter-spacing='0.08em' fill='#98a2b3'>2 ENCODE</text><text x='259' y='35' font-size='11' fill='#e6e8eb'>13 fixtures \u00b7 65 cases</text></g><path d='M466 26 L488 26' stroke='#96a3b5' stroke-width='1.1' marker-end='url(#ah3)'/><g class='stage' data-stage='3 ENFORCE'><title>3 ENFORCE \u00b7 repository checks \u00b7 the configured pre-commit checks; not a live verdict</title><rect x='492' y='4' width='214' height='44' rx='4' fill='#1b2027' stroke='#2a3038'/><rect x='492' y='4' width='3' height='44' fill='#5b8def'/><text x='503' y='17' font-size='10' letter-spacing='0.08em' fill='#98a2b3'>3 ENFORCE</text><text x='503' y='35' font-size='11' fill='#e6e8eb'>repository checks</text></g><path d='M710 26 L732 26' stroke='#96a3b5' stroke-width='1.1' marker-end='url(#ah3)'/><g class='stage' data-stage='4 RECORD'><title>4 RECORD \u00b7 6 capabilities \u00b7 each with the artefact that would refute it</title><rect x='736' y='4' width='214' height='44' rx='4' fill='#1b2027' stroke='#2a3038'/><rect x='736' y='4' width='3' height='44' fill='#5b8def'/><text x='747' y='17' font-size='10' letter-spacing='0.08em' fill='#98a2b3'>4 RECORD</text><text x='747' y='35' font-size='11' fill='#e6e8eb'>6 capabilities</text></g><path d='M954 26 L976 26' stroke='#96a3b5' stroke-width='1.1' marker-end='url(#ah3)'/><g class='stage' data-stage='5 ITERATE'><title>5 ITERATE \u00b7 0 found \u00b7 0 open \u00b7 the next run re-measures</title><rect x='980' y='4' width='214' height='44' rx='4' fill='#1b2027' stroke='#2a3038'/><rect x='980' y='4' width='3' height='44' fill='#5b8def'/><text x='991' y='17' font-size='10' letter-spacing='0.08em' fill='#98a2b3'>5 ITERATE</text><text x='991' y='35' font-size='11' fill='#e6e8eb'>0 found \u00b7 0 open</text></g><path d='M1087.0 48 C1168 62, 30 62, 111.0 48' fill='none' stroke='#a9b6c8' stroke-width='1.2' opacity='0.85' stroke-dasharray='4 3' marker-end='url(#ah3)'/><defs><marker id='ah3' viewBox='0 0 10 10' refX='8.5' refY='5' markerWidth='4' markerHeight='4' orient='auto'><path d='M0 1 L9 5 L0 9 z' fill='context-stroke'/></marker></defs></svg></div></div>\r\n     <div class='faults' id='faults'><b>FAULT</b>mlflow = UNOBSERVABLE \u00b7 dvc = UNOBSERVABLE \u00b7 quarto = UNOBSERVABLE \u00b7 decision_service = UNOBSERVABLE \u00b7 runtime_18434 = UNOBSERVABLE</div>\r\n-    <div id=\"source-provenance\"><p class='mono prov'>sources \u2014 current.json missing \u00b7 chains.json 13s \u00b7 recoveries missing \u00b7 pipeline.json 17.4h</p><p class=\"figure-note\">Source file ages; a quiet recovery log is not a failed service.</p></div>\r\n+    <div id=\"source-provenance\"><p class='mono prov'>sources \u2014 current.json missing \u00b7 chains.json 13s \u00b7 recoveries missing \u00b7 pipeline.json 18.7h</p><p class=\"figure-note\">Source file ages; a quiet recovery log is not a failed service.</p></div>\r\n   </section>\r\n   <div class=\"grid\">\r\n     <section class=\"card\" id=\"history\">\r\n       <h2>History \u2014 observed state transitions</h2>\r\n       <div id=\"strip\"><div class='srows'><div class='srow'><span class='sname'>decision</span><span class='scells'><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:03:27 \u00b7 PASS'></i><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:17:14 \u00b7 PASS'></i></span></div><div class='srow'><span class='sname'>demo (NO)</span><span class='scells'><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:03:27 \u00b7 PASS'></i><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:17:14 \u00b7 PASS'></i></span></div><div class='srow'><span class='sname'>diagnosis</span><span class='scells'><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:03:27 \u00b7 PASS'></i><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:17:14 \u00b7 PASS'></i></span></div><div class='srow'><span class='sname'>gates</span><span class='scells'><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:03:27 \u00b7 PASS'></i><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:17:14 \u00b7 PASS'></i></span></div><div class='srow'><span class='sname'>gates+project checker</span><span class='scells'><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#7d8590' title='18:03:27 \u00b7 SKIP'></i><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#7d8590' title='18:17:14 \u00b7 SKIP'></i></span></div><div class='srow'><span class='sname'>inference</span><span class='scells'><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:03:27 \u00b7 PASS'></i><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:17:14 \u00b7 PASS'></i></span></div><div class='srow'><span class='sname'>quarto</span><span class='scells'><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:03:27 \u00b7 PASS'></i><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:17:14 \u00b7 PASS'></i></span></div><div class='srow'><span class='sname'>registry</span><span class='scells'><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:03:27 \u00b7 PASS'></i><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:17:14 \u00b7 PASS'></i></span></div><div class='srow'><span class='sname'>surrogate (local NO)</span><span class='scells'><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:03:27 \u00b7 PASS'></i><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:17:14 \u00b7 PASS'></i></span></div><div class='srow'><span class='sname'>tracking</span><span class='scells'><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:03:27 \u00b7 PASS'></i><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:17:14 \u00b7 PASS'></i></span></div><div class='srow'><span class='sname'>validity (Gate S)</span><span class='scells'><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:03:27 \u00b7 PASS'></i><i class='sc' style='width:50.000%;background:#57ab5a' title='18:17:14 \u00b7 PASS'></i></span></div></div><div class='sax'><span>18:03:27</span><span>18:17:14</span><span>HKT</span></div><div class='gapsum'>no gaps in this window</div></div>\r\n-      <div id=\"evidence-freshness\"><div class='fresh'><span style='color:#d29922'>render 86.5 h (limit 24 h)</span> \u00b7 <span style='color:#7d8899'>operator evidence 90.6 h (limit 168 h)</span></div></div>\r\n+      <div id=\"evidence-freshness\"><div class='fresh'><span style='color:#d29922'>render 87.9 h (limit 24 h)</span> \u00b7 <span style='color:#7d8899'>operator evidence 92.0 h (limit 168 h)</span></div></div>\r\n     </section><section class='card' id='fault-ranking'><h2>Fault incidents \u2014 last 24 hours</h2><p class='empty'>No recorded incidents in this window.</p><p class='figure-note'>Recorded history, not active faults. Episodes are separated by more than 10 minutes; up to six nodes shown.</p></section>\r\n   </div>\r\n </main>\r","raw_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/raw/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/site%2Fdashboard.html","sha":"5d83d775b666eec1a7c28e762b48243015c237b5","status":"modified"},{"additions":50,"blob_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/blob/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/site%2Fdocs%2FDOWNSTREAM-QUICKSTART.md","changes":50,"contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Computational-social-science/Eidos/contents/site%2Fdocs%2FDOWNSTREAM-QUICKSTART.md?ref=045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae","deletions":0,"filename":"site/docs/DOWNSTREAM-QUICKSTART.md","patch":"@@ -1,5 +1,55 @@\n # Reuse EIDOS in an independent research project\n \n+## Current compatibility delivery, 2026-11-04\n+\n+The current qualified worker is **EIDOS Agent 0.5.0**, distribution `eidos`,\n+import namespace `framework`, consoles `eidos-agent` and `eidos`. Check the\n+[actual public release](https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/releases/tag/v0.5.0)\n+before downloading: source preparation or a version record is not publication.\n+The exact 51-module wheel passes native Windows and same-host offline Linux\n+numerical, lifecycle and recovery-shell acceptance. This supersedes the older\n+candidate selection below. The existing resident monitor remains separately on\n+0.4.12; installing a worker does not start or migrate it.\n+\n+Ordinary projects need neither a source fork nor a full checkout at execution\n+time. Use Python 3.12 and uv in a new, dedicated runtime directory. Preserve an\n+existing study's CUDA/PyTorch environment. Download the published wheel and the\n+frozen core requirements from its immutable tag, and verify both hashes before\n+installation. PowerShell, substituting actual absolute paths:\n+\n+```powershell\n+$runtime = '<new dedicated runtime directory>'\n+$project = '<existing research project root>'\n+New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $runtime -ErrorAction Stop | Out-Null\n+$wheel = Join-Path $runtime 'eidos-0.5.0-py3-none-any.whl'\n+$requirements = Join-Path $runtime 'core-requirements.txt'\n+Invoke-WebRequest 'https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/releases/download/v0.5.0/eidos-0.5.0-py3-none-any.whl' -OutFile $wheel\n+Invoke-WebRequest 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/v0.5.0/reference/numerical_programs_acceptance/recorded_trials/v0.5.0/input-linux/core-requirements.txt' -OutFile $requirements\n+if ((Get-FileHash $wheel -Algorithm SHA256).Hash -ne '56d2fe35b1e5ab552fe001ae675e3af4f095e78522fa8fae682f5ea41cfa301c') { throw 'Wheel identity mismatch' }\n+if ((Get-FileHash $requirements -Algorithm SHA256).Hash -ne 'ca27b7da8739f5e3f1d14e54a6172b1bc9bb9da9e4344b1103d9216b2378e5de') { throw 'Dependency lock identity mismatch' }\n+uv venv --python 3.12 (Join-Path $runtime 'venv')\n+$workerPy = Join-Path $runtime 'venv/Scripts/python.exe'\n+uv pip install --link-mode copy --python $workerPy --require-hashes -r $requirements\n+uv pip install --link-mode copy --python $workerPy --no-deps $wheel\n+& $workerPy -I -m framework.cli --help\n+& $workerPy -I -m framework.cli init --project $project --json\n+```\n+\n+On Linux use `venv/bin/python`; retain that venv entry rather than resolving its\n+base-interpreter symlink. These downloads require public network access; runtime\n+qualification itself can be offline. No model service, paid API or credential is\n+required for the core path. Initial scientific acceptance is deliberately REFUSED;\n+configure the project's own validator and declared inputs before running `check`.\n+Use the selected interpreter for `check/status/report/feedback`, as shown below.\n+Scientific validators and Quarto/TeX/Poppler prerequisites remain project-owned.\n+\n+The software repair campaign is documented in [feedback lifecycle](FEEDBACK-LIFECYCLE.md).\n+Use actual journal receipts to distinguish VALIDATED, RELEASED, ADOPTED, REPLAYED\n+and CLOSED. An installed package or Agent adapter alone cannot close a defect or\n+qualify scientific RSI. Public PyPI `eidos` belongs to an unrelated project.\n+\n+## Historical development checkpoints\n+\n Status: 2026-11-03. Stable release: **0.4.12**. The installed project CLI and\n shared-worker protocol below are **unreleased 0.5.0 development**. Installing a\n worker wheel does not install or migrate the complete monitor service.","raw_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/raw/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/site%2Fdocs%2FDOWNSTREAM-QUICKSTART.md","sha":"5407e36256c2412c56e233ef8e95dd39ae08c441","status":"modified"},{"additions":11,"blob_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/blob/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/site%2Fdocs%2FEVOLUTION.json","changes":18,"contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Computational-social-science/Eidos/contents/site%2Fdocs%2FEVOLUTION.json?ref=045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae","deletions":7,"filename":"site/docs/EVOLUTION.json","patch":"@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@\n {\n-  \"asof\": \"2026-11-04T10:14:21+08:00\",\n+  \"asof\": \"2026-11-04T11:34:33+08:00\",\n   \"version\": \"0.5.0\",\n   \"state\": {\n     \"chains\": {\n@@ -51,16 +51,12 @@\n     \"open_defects\": 0\n   },\n   \"evolution\": {\n-    \"mutation_runs\": 2,\n+    \"mutation_runs\": 6,\n     \"runs_with_a_blind_spot\": 0,\n     \"blind_spots_found\": 0,\n     \"blind_spots_open\": 0,\n-    \"releases\": 22,\n+    \"releases\": 23,\n     \"tests_by_release\": [\n-      {\n-        \"version\": \"0.4.7\",\n-        \"tests\": 786\n-      },\n       {\n         \"version\": \"0.4.8\",\n         \"tests\": 876\n@@ -80,9 +76,17 @@\n       {\n         \"version\": \"0.4.12\",\n         \"tests\": 1208\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \"version\": \"0.5.0\",\n+        \"tests\": 1365\n       }\n     ],\n     \"blind_spots_by_run\": [\n+      0,\n+      0,\n+      0,\n+      0,\n       0,\n       0\n     ]","raw_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/raw/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/site%2Fdocs%2FEVOLUTION.json","sha":"8f8e837d3cc0f38cfe1ac9016aea161b489f3725","status":"modified"},{"additions":15,"blob_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/blob/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/site%2Fdocs%2FFEEDBACK-LIFECYCLE.md","changes":15,"contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Computational-social-science/Eidos/contents/site%2Fdocs%2FFEEDBACK-LIFECYCLE.md?ref=045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae","deletions":0,"filename":"site/docs/FEEDBACK-LIFECYCLE.md","patch":"@@ -147,3 +147,18 @@ The same 51-module wheel also passes the current native Windows and isolated\n Linux numerical/lifecycle/recovery-shell acceptance. Linux additionally checks\n both console aliases and the old/repaired private probe. The current artifact's\n Linux evidence is now independent of the earlier wheel's historical profile.\n+\n+### First exact-head CI refusal and test-contract correction\n+\n+The first delivery head `21e26b784604616a96648a615f48aa2747f35e7f` passed the\n+Windows/Linux installed-SDK workflow but failed both Linux source suites. The\n+registration test incorrectly resolved the venv launch entry to the base Python,\n+contrary to the existing SDK and deployment contract. Publication stopped before\n+tagging. An independent normal-installed, network-disabled Linux replay retained\n+the original one-failure/four-pass result. Correcting the expected launch entry\n+and independently asserting the actual worker prefix yields five passes on\n+Linux and five on Windows. Both focused independent reviews approve the change.\n+The wheel, SDK and sealed campaign producer/policy are unchanged. Frozen raw CI\n+annotations, old/new test inputs and actual execution evidence are retained in\n+`reference/shared_monitor_acceptance/recorded_trials/venv-entry-ci-v1`.\n+Remote CI must pass the new exact delivery head before publication can proceed.","raw_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/raw/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/site%2Fdocs%2FFEEDBACK-LIFECYCLE.md","sha":"8d18aac80303cf27796b2482331103fc83ded402","status":"modified"},{"additions":0,"blob_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/blob/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/site%2Fdocs%2Fscreens%2Fweb%2Findex-top.webp","changes":0,"contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Computational-social-science/Eidos/contents/site%2Fdocs%2Fscreens%2Fweb%2Findex-top.webp?ref=045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae","deletions":0,"filename":"site/docs/screens/web/index-top.webp","raw_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/raw/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/site%2Fdocs%2Fscreens%2Fweb%2Findex-top.webp","sha":"a1521880cba45868b0d8be1874f9018b224e83b3","status":"modified"},{"additions":9,"blob_url":"https://github.com/Computational-social-science/Eidos/blob/045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae/site%2Findex.html","changes":18,"contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Computational-social-science/Eidos/contents/site%2Findex.html?ref=045c9e08b1f0aceff2e63a23ab77e121c141c6ae","deletions":9,"filename":"site/index.html","patch":"@@ -284,7 +284,7 @@\n   <span class=\"hchip\">11 chains \u00b7 1365 tests</span>\r\n   <a class=\"cta\" href=\"http://127.0.0.1:8765/\">Monitor \u2192</a>\r\n </div></header>\r\n-<div class=\"shell\"><nav class=\"rail\" aria-label=\"Sections\"><ol><li><a href=\"#position\"><span>01</span>Academic proposition</a></li><li><a href=\"#evidence\"><span>02</span>Measured evidence</a></li><li><a href=\"#demo\"><span>03</span>Softmax case study</a></li><li><a href=\"#pipeline\"><span>04</span>Research method</a></li><li><a href=\"#models\"><span>05</span>Model capability limits</a></li><li><a href=\"#gates\"><span>06</span>Validity checks</a></li><li><a href=\"#research\"><span>07</span>Research agenda</a></li><li><a href=\"#architecture\"><span>08</span>Architecture</a></li><li><a href=\"#orchestration\"><span>09</span>Orchestration</a></li><li><a href=\"#state\"><span>10</span>Verification ledger</a></li><li><a href=\"#monitor\"><span>11</span>Live operations</a></li><li><a href=\"#start\"><span>12</span>Use & reproduce</a></